     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hi,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">I have a question regarding the key of exercise (5) of chapter 4,\r\nreproduced below:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:4.0pt;text-autospace:none\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"><font size=\"2\">(5)   50 students took a statistics\r\nexam, the average (!) result was 77% (standard deviation 10.3). What is the\r\n99%-confidence interval for this result? <u></u><u></u></font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:4.0pt;text-autospace:none\"><font size=\"2\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">se</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\"> &lt;- </span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">0.103</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">/sqrt(</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">50</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:4.0pt;text-autospace:none\"><font size=\"2\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">tvalue</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\"> &lt;- qt(</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">0.005</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">, </span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">df</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">=</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">49</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">, </span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">lower.tail</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">=</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(181,118,12)\">FALSE</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:4.0pt;text-autospace:none\"><font size=\"2\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">77</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">-(</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">se</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">*</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">tvalue</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">) </span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"># lower limit of the 99%-confidence interval<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">77</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">+(</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">se</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">*</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:black\">tvalue</span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(7,0,135)\">) </span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"># upper limit\r\nof the 99%-confidence interval</span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">I can’t figure out why the sd to calculate\r\nthe </span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"><font size=\"2\">se</font></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></span><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"color:black\">is\r\n0.103 and not 10.3. I could make sense of it if the mean used in the\r\ncalculation for the lower and upper limits of the CI was 0.77 (since it’s a\r\npercentage), but not with 77 as is the case in the code here. Am I missing\r\nsomething?</span><span style=\"color:black;font-size:11pt\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"color:black\">Thanks in advance for any help!</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Samantha</span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
